/* book: lead: In CMOS, the source diffusions, the well and the substrate form a hidden four-layer p-n-p-n switch. A current spike can forward-bias one of its junctions. If the parasitic npn and pnp transistors have enough gain and the well and substrate resistances are large enough, they feed each other and the supply rails short together. This is latch-up, and it can destroy or reset a chip. Layout prevents it */
