/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - In an n-well CMOS process, every PMOS sits inside an n-well and every NMOS sits in the p-substrate.
   - Two parasitic bipolar transistors appear inside that stack.
   - The collector of each transistor drives the base of the other.
   - Latch-up needs a trigger.
   - Vsub = Isub × Rsub, Vwell = IC,npn × Rwell, βnpn × βpnp > 1
   - Vsub is how far the substrate rises above VSS and Vwell is how far the well falls below VDD (V).
   - Both emitters must be forward biased for the loop to close.
   - Layout is the first defence.
   - Process choices lower the resistances further.
*/
